' F2 -- Positioning within the surrounding solution space.
' Chapter 2 (Foundations / Related Work). Concept diagram.
' Claim supported: the system occupies the gap between document-conversion
' tooling (structure without pedagogy) and learning platforms (pedagogy
' without ingestion) -- it derives assessable objects from raw lecture PDFs.
'
' NOTE FOR THE AUTHOR: the four quadrant families below are grounded in this
' system's own capabilities and its actual dependency set. The specific named
' exemplars you cite in each family must come from YOUR related-work reading --
' do not present this figure as a literature survey it is not.
@startuml f2-positioning
!include _style.iuml

title Positioning: structure versus pedagogy

skinparam rectangle {
  BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
}

rectangle "**Document conversion / layout AI**\nPDF to markup or markdown\n----\nRecovers //structure//: pages, blocks,\ntables, reading order.\nProduces no assessable objects.\nNo learner model.\n\n//This system consumes tools from this\nfamily: PyMuPDF for extraction, and\nMarkItDown / LlamaParse / MinerU /\nOpenDataLoader as swappable text\nfront-ends.//" as DOC #F2F2F2

rectangle "**Learning platforms / LMS**\ncourses, enrolment, grading\n----\nRich //pedagogy//: assignments,\nprogress, analytics, spaced review.\nAssumes content is **already**\nauthored and structured.\nIngestion is a manual upload." as LMS #F2F2F2

rectangle "**Retrieval-augmented QA**\ngrounded answers over a corpus\n----\nAnswers //questions// over documents.\nOptimises faithfulness and citation.\nDoes not durably materialise\nreusable learning objects." as RAG #F2F2F2

rectangle "**THIS WORK**\nlecture materials to structured\neducational content\n----\n• ingests raw slide decks as the //primary// input\n• materialises persistent, addressable objects:\n  slides, MCQs with Bloom levels, embeddings\n• layers pedagogy on the derived objects:\n  grounded tutor, SM-2 review, mock exams\n• keeps a human-in-the-loop correction path\n• server-authoritative: the database defines\n  what a slide //is// once parsed" as THIS #BFBFBF

DOC -[#1A1A1A]-> THIS : "structure,\nbut no pedagogy"
LMS -[#1A1A1A]-> THIS : "pedagogy,\nbut no ingestion"
RAG -[#1A1A1A]-> THIS : "grounded answers,\nbut nothing persisted"

note bottom of THIS
  The distinguishing move is **materialisation**. A RAG system
  answers a question and forgets; this pipeline writes durable
  objects that several independent features then consume — the
  same quiz_questions rows feed in-lecture quizzes, the SRS card
  factory (with no further LLM call) and mock-exam sampling.
  One extraction, many pedagogical uses.
end note

note as CAVEAT
  **Author's note — not a literature survey.**
  These four families are derived from this system's
  own capabilities and dependency set, not from a
  citation search. Populate each family with the
  specific works you cite in Chapter 2, and check
  that the boundaries still hold once you do.
end note

CAVEAT .. DOC

legend bottom
  Grayscale-safe: families are distinguished by position and label, not by fill.
endlegend

@enduml
